  13:     - A single divider color fills the center column except for the center marker.
  14:     - All remaining foreground pixels form the object to copy, entirely on the left side of the divider.
  15:     Rule
  16:     - Keep the input unchanged.
  17:     - For every object pixel, paint the pixel rotated 180 degrees around the center marker with the same color.
  18:     Key insight
  19:     - The center marker is the rotation center; the yellow-looking divider is not mirrored, it only separates the source from the empty target side.
  20:     """
